      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = x^3 + x^2 - 8x + 7$ to get $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 + 2x - 8$.",
        "Solve $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\implies (3x - 4)(x + 2) = 0$ for $x = -2, \\frac{4}{3}$.",
        "Identify $a = -2$ and $b = \\frac{4}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the curve equation with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 + 2x - 8$$",
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$ to find the stationary points:\n$$3x^2 + 2x - 8 = 0 \\implies (3x - 4)(x + 2) = 0 \\implies x = -2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = \\frac{4}{3}$$",
        "The open interval containing no stationary points between these two locations is $-2 < x < \\frac{4}{3}$:\n$$\\text{Least possible value: } a = -2$$\n$$\\text{Greatest possible value: } b = \\frac{4}{3}$$"
      ],
